	In pl10, named weapons cost lots more than other weapons do. This
can be abused if you find a two-handed sword or elven dagger in a shop: 
you buy the weapon, name it, and resell it at a profit. 

	If a shop is generated with one of these two weapons, it should
automatically make the named weapon if it isn't already in the game. After
all, why would the shopkeeper pass up the chance to improve the value of
his merchandise? Or if he bought it from an adventurer, wouldn't the 
adventurer have named the weapon in order to sell it at a higher price?
In this way the loophole would be closed.

